---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// Privacy policy for the Slumbio iPhone app. App Store Connect requires a
// URL; the app links here from Settings and from the paywall.
const updated = 'September 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy · Slumbio" description="What Slumbio does with your data. Nothing." noindex puck={false}>
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Slumbio · updated {updated}</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">Slumbio has no account, no server and no analytics. Nothing you do in it leaves your phone.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="body">
    <h2>What the app stores</h2>
    <p>
      Your settings, saved mixes, breathing preferences and the sleep journal
      are written to the app's own folder on your phone. They are included in
      your iCloud or iTunes device backup like any other app data. Deleting the
      app deletes them.
    </p>

    <h2>What the app sends</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. The app makes no network requests. There is no crash reporting,
      no usage tracking, no advertising identifier, and no third-party code
      that phones home.
    </p>

    <h2>Purchases</h2>
    <p>
      Slumbio Plus is sold through Apple's in-app purchase system. Apple
      handles payment and knows what you bought; I receive aggregate sales
      figures from Apple and nothing about you personally. Subscriptions can be
      managed or cancelled in Settings › Apple Account › Subscriptions on your
      phone.
    </p>

    <h2>Notifications</h2>
    <p>
      If you turn on the sunrise alarm, the bedtime reminder, or start a free
      week, the app schedules local notifications on your phone. They are
      created and delivered by iOS on the device. No notification server is
      involved.
    </p>

    <h2>Health</h2>
    <p>Slumbio does not read or write Health data.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Slumbio is not directed at children under 13 and collects no data from anyone.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If any of this changes, the date at the top will, and the app will say
      so before it does anything new.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Brett Boggs, <a href="mailto:brettmboggs@gmail.com">brettmboggs@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <a class="back-link" href="/slumbio/">&larr; Slumbio</a>
</Base>

<style>
  .body {
    max-width: 38rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 3rem;
  }
  .body h2 {
    margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }
  .body p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
</style>
